{"study_accession":"PRJNA877113","secondary_study_accession":"SRP395814","title":"The two enantiomers of 2-hydroxyglutarate differentially regulate cytotoxic T cell function","description":"2-hydroxyglutarate (2HG) is a by-product of the TCA cycle, and is readily detected in the tissues of healthy individuals. 2HG is found in two enantiomeric forms: S-2HG and R-2HG. Here, we investigate the differential roles of these two enantiomers in CD8+ T cell biology, where we found they had highly divergent effects on proliferation, differentiation, and T cell function. We show here an analysis of structural determinants that likely underlie these differential effects on specific a-ketoglutarate (aKG)-dependent enzymes. Treatment of CD8+ T cells with exogenous S-2HG, but not R-2HG, increased CD8+ T cell fitness in vivo, and enhanced anti-tumour activity. These data show that S-2HG and R-2HG should be considered as two distinct and important actors in the regulation of T cell function. Overall design: Comparative gene expression of CD8+ T cells treated with S- or R-2HG. All samples are in (biological) triplicates. Controls are H2O/vehicle.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":21,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN30685051","study_accession":"PRJNA877113","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"CD8+ T cells 12d activation (H2O) donor 3","description":"CD8+ T cells 12d activation (H2O) donor 3","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6544278","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-07-23","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["individual","different donor 3"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","CD8+ T cells"],["treatment","H2O"],["time","12d activation"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR21434163","experiment_accession":"SRX17438318","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":40000111,"base_count":3360009324,"first_public":"2023-07-23","experime